# Files that RUN on the Linux VM must keep LF endings, whatever a Windows
# checkout would otherwise do to them. A shell script that reaches the VM with
# CRLF fails with the classic "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M" — and the ones here
# are the backup loop and the restore, which is the worst possible place to
# discover it. Scoped to these patterns on purpose: a blanket `* text=auto`
# would renormalise the whole repo in one unreviewable diff.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.conf          text eol=lf
*.inc           text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
docker-compose*.yml text eol=lf
*.sql           text eol=lf
